    <tags>pull-vids video downloader youtube yt-dlp cli golang</tags>
    <summary>Universal video downloader CLI supporting 1000+ websites</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
pull-vids is a command-line video downloader built on yt-dlp, supporting YouTube,
Vimeo, Twitter/X, TikTok, Instagram and 1000+ other sites.

### Fast by default

Google's CDN rate-limits each TCP connection independently, so a single-stream
download leaves a fast link mostly idle. pull-vids downloads over several
connections at once, which scales throughput close to linearly:

| Connections | Throughput |
|-------------|------------|
| 1           | 3.3 MB/s   |
| 8           | 25.8 MB/s  |
| 16          | 48.7 MB/s  |
| 32          | 95.2 MB/s  |

Use `-N 16` to raise the connection count. The tool backs off automatically if
the server starts rejecting requests.

### Features

* 1000+ supported sites via yt-dlp
* Quality selection from 360p through 2160p
* Audio-only extraction to mp3/m4a
* Playlist downloads
* Browser cookie support for authenticated content

### Dependencies

ffmpeg, yt-dlp and aria2 are installed automatically as package dependencies.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/vib795/pull-vids/releases</releaseNotes>

    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="ffmpeg" />
      <dependency id="yt-dlp" />
      <dependency id="aria2" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
